ach element appears once.\n\nLet's enumerate systematically.\n\nWe can consider cases based on whether we include E or not.\n\nCase 1: Include E ([3,4]). Then 3 and 4 are covered. We cannot include any other row that contains 3 or 4. So cannot include C ([3]), B ([4]), H ([2,3]), or E again. So remaining rows allowed: A ([2]), D ([0]), F ([0,1]), G ([1]). Need to cover 0,1,2. 2 must be covered by A (since H not allowed). So A must be included. That covers 2. Now we need 0 and 1. Options: D covers 0, F covers 0,1, G covers 1. We need to cover 0 and 1 exactly once. Let's consider combinations:\n\n- Use D ([0]) and G ([1]) -> covers 0 and 1"}}],"created":1790939729,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4185,"total_tokens":4953,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-9f8x6eL6WUgxMkofJHcAvUvtenDwG8jv","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4185,"prompt_ms":540.797,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12922270011947432,"prompt_per_second":7738.578431463192,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2418.624,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.1533559322033895,"predicted_per_second":317.12246302029587}}